// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6502 Add Radmin DLL sideloading detection rule
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6502
// Pull request author: brandolphj
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Radmin DLL Sideloading From User AppData
// Sigma ID: 7b9139bc-caba-464b-a932-dc7e1dca6eb9
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: brandolphj
// Date: 2026-10-21 | Modified: 2026-11-18
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1574.001
// Description: Detects potential DLL search-order hijacking involving the legitimate Radmin executable
//   FamItrfc.exe loading BlkScrDl.dll from the user's AppData\Local\Radmin directory. Google Threat
//   Intelligence Group/Mandiant documented this activity during the AOMEI Backupper supply-chain
//   compromise. The compromised update process delivered a Radmin bundle containing a legitimate
//   signed executable and an attacker-controlled BlkScrDl.dll, which was loaded through DLL search-
//   order hijacking. The rule specifically targets the reported AppData location to reduce false
//   positives. During limited local testing of the official Radmin Server 3.5.2.1 installer,
//   FamItrfc.exe was found under System32\rserver30, while BlkScrDl.dll was not found in the
//   extracted Server or Viewer installers.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/investigating-ephemeral-supply-chain-tampering
//   - https://www.manageengine.com/threat-analysis-lab/aomei-backupper-supply-chain-compromise.html
//   - https://labs.cloudsecurityalliance.org/research/csa-research-note-aomei-backupper-update-server-tampering-20/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/3f2111066d0466ae07a113731be797e6b9c4944f/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_side_load_radmin_dll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceImageLoadEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\AppData\\Local\\Radmin\\FamItrfc.exe" and FolderPath endswith "\\AppData\\Local\\Radmin\\BlkScrDl.dll"
